# OWNERSHIP.map — who decides what, keyed on CONCERN (never on file alone).
# Read by kernel/ownership-lint.sh; location is PF_OWNERSHIP_MAP in the profile.
#
# WHY CONCERN AND NOT FILE
#   A per-file map marks most of a shared application contested, and blocks a
#   correct, agreed cross-concern change (a project-wide palette swap, say). A
#   map that is overridden once is ignored forever. The real boundary is
#   "A owns the colour tokens in EVERY file; B owns the business logic in the
#   production files" — a concern axis. So a lane is (owner x concern x glob).
#
# FORMAT (whitespace-separated)   <mode> <owner> <concern> <glob>   [# note]
#   mode     own        this owner decides at this concern: ok for the owner,
#                       STOP for others
#            shared     both build here by design: WARN, deploy per file, verify
#            contested  both have landed here and nobody has ruled: WARN, open a
#                       handoff item BEFORE editing
#            frozen     no build decision may change it: STOP, owner ruling
#                       required — the one wall a RATIFIED receipt cannot open
#            (unmapped) undescribed: WARN — describe it, or say why it has none
#   owner    a dev initial from the profile's DEVS, or * for any/both
#   concern  one of the profile's PF_CONCERNS (or *)
#   glob     repo-relative glob, or table:<name> for a data surface
#
# 'contested' IS NOT A FAILURE STATE. It is the honest label for a boundary
# nobody has decided yet; naming it turns a silent collision into a scheduled
# decision.
#
# THE ESCAPE HATCH IS A RECEIPT, NOT A GATE. Cross-concern work is legitimate.
# Put a `RATIFIED: <who>, <when>` line in the commit message (or pass
# --ratified). The linter cannot verify it; it records that the claim was made
# and lists every lane crossed, so the owners who must smoke-test can be named.
# What is protected is ATTENTION, not permission.
#
# MATCH SEMANTICS
#   - A path can match SEVERAL lanes at different concerns; every matching lane
#     is reported.
#   - One glob per line. Matching is shell `case` pattern matching: braces
#     {a,b} are literal here and will not match. Write two lines.
#   - Put broad catch-alls FIRST and specific carve-outs LAST.
#   - Evidence is generated, lanes are ruled: `ownership-lint.sh --refresh`
#     recomputes per-lane commit counts from git and prints CONTRADICTED when a
#     lane's evidence disagrees with its owner. It never edits a lane.
#
# EXAMPLE (neutral; replace with your own lanes)

# 0. Catch-all, broadest first: B owns visual tokens in every file.
own   b  style      *

# A. Application logic.
own   a  logic      src/billing/*
own   a  logic      src/ops/*
own   b  style      src/views/*.css
shared  *  nav      src/views/layout.*
contested  *  logic  src/shared/*

# B. Data surfaces.
own   a  schema     table:invoices

# C. Frozen until the owner rules.
frozen  a  fiscal   src/billing/tax-seal.*
